# Server-side env for resume Smart parse (Gemini).
# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill in the key.
# The `.env*` files are gitignored, so the key stays local.
#
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — Gemini 2.5 Flash + Flash-Lite
# both have a free tier that is enough for development.
#
# Do NOT prefix the variable with VITE_. The VITE_ prefix exposes a var to the
# browser bundle; we want this key to stay on the server side only. The Vite
# dev plugin at `server/parse-resume-dev-plugin.ts` reads it from the
# process env at dev-server startup, and the Cloudflare Pages Function at
# `functions/api/parse-resume.ts` reads it from the Cloudflare env binding.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: comma-separated origin allowlist for the Cloudflare Pages Function.
# Leave unset in dev. In production, set to e.g.
#   https://resume-by-temi.pages.dev,https://resume.example.com
# Dev (Vite middleware) skips this check entirely.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
